hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1322","Aslam said, \ 'Umar ibn al-Khattab said"," 'Do not let your love\nbe a total infatuation. Do not let your anger be destruction.' I asked","\n'How is that?' He replied"," 'When you love"," you are infatuated like a child.\nWhen you hate"," you desire destruction for your companion.'\"""""
"1323","Sayyidunā Abū Hurayrah (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu) narrates that the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallAllāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: \The strong and brave one is not the one who overpowers (others in wrestling); rather"," the truly strong one is the one who controls himself at the time of anger.\""\n\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1323 | Arabic Hadith: 1323"""
"1324","Sayyidunā Ibn ʿUmar (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhumā) narrates, and he said: \There is no drink that a person consumes which"," in the sight of Allāh"," carries greater reward and recompense than the drink that a person consumes seeking the pleasure of Allāh.\""\n\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1324 | Arabic Hadith: 1324"""
"1325","Sayyidunā Sulaymān ibn Ṣard (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu) narrates, and he said: Two men reviled one another in the presence of the Prophet (ṣallAllāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam), and one of them became so enraged that his face turned red. The Prophet (ṣallAllāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam), upon seeing him, said: \Indeed"," I know a word which"," if this person were to say it"," his anger would subside. (That word is): Aʿūdhu billāhi min al-Shayṭān al-Rajīm (I seek refuge in Allāh from the accursed Shayṭān).\"" So a man got up"," went to that person"," and said: \""Do you know what the Prophet (ṣallAllāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said? He said: 'You should recite: Aʿūdhu billāhi min al-Shayṭān al-Rajīm.'\"" That man replied: \""Do you think I am insane?\""\n\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1325 | Arabic Hadith: 1325"""
"1326","Sulaymān ibn Ṣard (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu) narrates, and he said: I was sitting in the presence of the Prophet (ṣallAllāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) and two men were reviling one another. The face of one of them turned red and his veins swelled. The Prophet (ṣallAllāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: \Indeed"," I know a word which"," if this person were to say it"," all his anger would be extinguished.\"" So the people said to him: \""The Prophet (ṣallAllāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: 'Seek refuge in Allāh from the accursed Shayṭān.'\"" He replied: \""Am I some madman?\""\n\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1326 | Arabic Hadith: 1326"""
"1327","Sayyidunā Ibn ʿAbbās (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhumā) narrates that the Messenger of Allāh (ṣallAllāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said: \Teach the people the religion and make things easy; teach and adopt the easy approach.\"" The Prophet (ṣallAllāhu ʿalayhi wa sallam) said this three times"," and then said: \""And when you become angry"," remain silent.\"" He said this twice.\n\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1327 | Arabic Hadith: 1327"""
"1328","ʿUbayd al-Kindī (raḥimahullāh) narrates that he heard Sayyidunā ʿAlī (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu) saying to Ibn Kawwāʾ: \Do you know what the early people used to say?\"" (He said:) \""When you love someone"," do not go to excess in your love"," for it may be that one day that very person becomes your enemy. And when you harbour enmity towards someone"," do not go to excess in your enmity"," for it may be that one day that very person becomes your friend.\""\n\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1328 | Arabic Hadith: 1328"""
"1329","Sayyidunā ʿUmar ibn al-Khaṭṭāb (raḍiyAllāhu ʿanhu) narrates, and he said: \Let not your love drive you to madness"," and let not your enmity drive you to destruction.\"" I asked: \""How is that?\"" He replied: \""It is that when you love"," you love with the reckless love of a child"," taking everything to be solely for that person; and when you harbour enmity"," you wish that your enemy be utterly destroyed.\""\n\nAl-Adab al-Mufrad"," Hadith: 1329 | Arabic Hadith: 1329"""
